sed": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`/-/tasks` and `/-/tasks.json` now exist. They're gated by `permissions-debug` and built like `/-/threads`. The check command passes (240 passed, 3 xpassed). I read through the implementer's diff and found nothing to fix. I didn't edit the three test files.\n\n- **Supervisor:** `BackgroundTask.plugin` and `_resolve_plugin_name` are gone. `BackgroundTask.function` holds the callable's dotted path, which `_function_path` computes (partials unwrapped, callable instances reported as `Class.__call__`). The supervisor also has a read-only `launched` property.\n- **App:** `_tasks()` sits next to `_threads` and returns `tasks` and `launched`. The new route is right after `/-/threads`, and the `add_background_task` docstring names `.function`.\n- **Docs:** `docs/introspection.rst` has a new `/-/tasks` section with an example response, and `docs/internals.rst` lists `.function` instead of `.plugin`.\n\nThe implementer also added `/-/tasks` to the list of debug endpoints exempt from the JSON stability promise in `docs/introspection.rst`. The spec didn't ask for that line, so you may want to drop it.", "ttft_ms": 1816, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 16820, "uuid": "c86f7225-213f-4e80-a678-b2357bbb4919", "ttft_stream_ms": 1250, "time_to_request_ms": 20, "first_content_frame_ms": 1250, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
